            </encodings>
            <customized-tooltip>
              <formatted-text>
                <run>Cohort Date is defined as the date when a vendor activated Auto Accept &amp; we aggregate behaviors of vendors who have the same Cohort (Cohort date or Cohort week) to observe their performance development before and after Auto Accept Activation. 

</run>
                <run italic='true'>For the sake of simplicity, we assume the Auto Accept Activation date is the first time a vendor received an order with Auto Accept configurations.</run>
                <run>

When t-dimension Granularity filter is &apos;Weekly&apos;:
T-2 cohort includes 14-8 days before Auto Accept Activation date
T-1 cohort includes 7 days before Auto Accept Activation date
T1 cohort includes Auto Accept Activation date and 6 days later
T2 cohort includes 7-13 days after Auto Accept Activation date
.. and so on</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='mark'>
                <format attr='shape' value='My Shapes/info-icon.png' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
        </panes>
